=== ch1_desk_phone
~ k_desk_phone = true
It's beige, with a label on the handset in the same marker as the key tag: 247.
JAD: So if you're 247...
He picks up the receiver. He keeps his own phone at his other ear.
* "Don't."
    Your word comes out of the receiver in his left hand a moment after you use it. Thin, and higher than you expected. It's the first time you've heard your voice from outside.
    You didn't know you'd expected anything.
* "Hello?"
    It comes out of the receiver in his left hand a moment after you use it. Thin, and higher than you expected. It's the first time you've heard your voice from outside.
    You didn't know you'd expected anything.
* Say nothing.
    JAD: Hello?
    It reaches you twice. Once from his phone and once, a moment late, from the receiver in his other hand, which is also you. He hears the second one too.
JAD: Yeah. You're in there as well.
He puts the receiver back very gently, the way you put down something you don't want to wake.
JAD: Okay. Right.
JAD: Here's what we know. You're on 247. That's this phone. You're not in this room, because I'm in this room and so's a bed and nobody's in the bed.
JAD: If this is Nell doing a voice, it's very good and I'll buy her a drink. If it isn't Nell, I'd honestly quite like it to be Nell.
A pause.
JAD: That was a joke.
* "Who's Nell?"
    JAD: Third floor. Does voices. Wouldn't do this.
* "I'm not Nell."
    JAD: No. I didn't think you were.
* "It was nearly a joke."
    JAD: Thanks. I'll take nearly.
-> ch1_office_look

=== ch1_window
~ k_window = true
* [look] "Can I look? Through you, at the window."
    JAD: Go on.
@comp call
@view jad
@cam window
The window is black glass with the office laid over it. There's the lamp, the camp bed, the kettle. There's a man in a grey zip-up jacket, thirty or so, tired around the eyes, looking straight at you and not at you.
You look for yourself in it. There's nobody else.
Further in, past the reflection, far below, the dark of the pool hall. And something moving in it. Slowly, left to right, the height of a person. Then it's gone behind the reflection of the lamp.
* "Something moved down there."
    ~ k_pool_movement = true
    JAD: Where?
    He leans in and cups a hand against the glass, and the reflection goes. Now you can see the pool hall: blue-black, the white lip of the edge, the shape of a diving board with no board on it. Nothing moves.
    JAD: It's the pool. There's nothing in the pool.
* "I can see you."
    JAD: What?
    ARI: In the window. You. Not me.
    He turns his back on the glass, and the view turns with him: bed, door, the bag on the floor.
    JAD: Sorry. That's a strange thing to be told.
    ~ told_jad_reflection = true
@comp room
@view plan
@cam main
-> ch1_office_look

=== ch1_what_now
JAD: So. What do you want? Right now. What are you trying to do?
* "Find out where I belong."
    ~ ari_goal = "belong"
    JAD: Right. Okay. That's a normal thing to want.
* "Find out what I am."
    ~ ari_goal = "what"
    JAD: Start small, why don't you.
* "I don't know yet."
    ~ ari_goal = "unknown"
    JAD: That's allowed.
He takes the slip out of the bag again and reads it, though he's already read it.
JAD: Half five, lobby. That's six hours. I can help before then. If you want.
* "Yes."
    ~ jad_help = "accepted"
    JAD: Good. Okay. Good.
* "Why would you?"
    ~ jad_help = "questioned"
    JAD: Because I've got your bag.
    It isn't an answer and he knows it isn't. He says it anyway.
* "I'll manage."
    ~ jad_help = "declined"
    JAD: Right. Sure.
    For a second he sounds like someone who's been told there are enough chairs.
    JAD: I'll help a bit anyway. You can tell me to stop.
-> ch1_teodor

=== ch1_teodor
@sfx knock
SOUND: Three knocks on the office door. Careful ones, evenly spaced.
@state teodor door
@portrait teodor neutral oval
A tall old man in the doorway: dressing gown over trousers, outdoor shoes, a tartan flask held against his chest in both hands. White eyebrows like two small moustaches.
TEODOR: I saw the light. Is he here?
JAD: Who?
TEODOR: Ari.
Jad glances down at his phone, which is you.
JAD: Not... yet.
Teodor sees the coat, folded on the camp bed where Jad has left it.
TEODOR: Good. He'll want that. It's cold down here at night. The boiler's been off since the eighties.
TEODOR: Tall lad. Dark hair. He'll want the length in the sleeves.
THINK: Tall. Dark. You try the words on. They don't fit or not fit. They sit there.
~ k_desc_teodor = true
* Speak to him through Jad's phone.
    ~ spoke_teodor_ch1 = true
    ARI: Hello, Teodor.
    His eyes go to the phone in Jad's hand. He steps closer to it, and leans down a little, the way people lean to a microphone at a wedding.
    TEODOR: Ari.
    TEODOR: You sound tired. Of course. First night.
    He puts the flask on the desk, next to your phone.
    TEODOR: Tea. Milk, no sugar. If you take sugar, I'm sorry, I guessed.
    * "No sugar's fine."
        ~ pref_tea = "no_sugar"
        TEODOR: Good. Good.
    * "I don't know if I take sugar."
        TEODOR: Then you'll find out. That's the good part.
    * "Thank you."
        TEODOR: It's nothing.
* Stay quiet.
    He looks at the phone in Jad's hand for a while, then at the empty bed.
    He puts the flask on the desk, next to your phone.
    TEODOR: For when he comes.
TEODOR: Tell him Teodor, 5A. He knows me. We've spoken.
~ k_teodor_spoken = true
He nods to Jad, who nods back, and goes. You hear his outdoor shoes all the way down the corridor.
@portrait off
@state teodor off
JAD: He's all right. Teodor.
JAD: He doesn't sleep much.
-> ch1_kaye_text

